FINAL ANSWER:
## Bus factor: 2 for the whole repo, but only 1 among active authors

**Scope:** whole repository, 1,662 non-blank lines (1,995 counting blank lines, per the merged run; the brief says 1,985, see below).

- **Bus factor (50% of lines): 2.** Troy Goode (649 lines, 39.0%, merged) and Douglas Christopher Wilson (551 lines, 33.2%) together hold 72.2%. On the unmerged brief figures it is also 2: Troy 605 (36.4%) and Douglas 551 (33.2%).
- **To reach 80%: 4 authors** (merged). The unmerged brief says 5.
- **Counting blank lines:** bus factor 2 (Troy 40.8% plus Douglas 31.7% = 72.5%).
- **Active bus factor: 1.** Troy Goode alone holds at least half of the 860 lines held by the 9 authors active in the last 365 days. This is counted on the active lines, not all lines.
- **Activity:** `as of 2026-04-12: 9 of 44 authors committed in the last 365 days and hold 51.7% of the non-blank lines; 48.3% of the lines belong to people with no commit in that time`.

Troy Goode's merge of two addresses is a strong suggestion from the tool, not a confirmed fact. It is a guess from names and addresses (<email redacted> and troy@laptop.example). I did not write a `.mailmap` because you did not ask for one.

### Top owners (merged view, `--merge-identities`)

| Author | Lines (share) | Counting blank lines | Commits | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses) | 649 (39.0%) | 810 (40.8%) | 95 (30.2%) | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 551 (33.2%) | 629 (31.7%) | 143 (45.4%) | 2021-09-07 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 80 (4.8%) | 95 (4.8%) | 2 (0.6%) | 2024-05-14 |
